Subject: [PATCH] Launch load: five sign-ups researched at once; enrichment
 four at a time, 200 a day per owner
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the tester's launch report (60358, F9 and F10), on Misho's yes to Q6 and
Q7 (15 Oct). Registration research took one user a minute, so 200 sign-ups
waited 200 minutes: five workers now each take the next queued user as soon
as they finish, topped up every 30 s. Contact enrichment ran two at a time
with no limit per owner, so a hundred phonebooks meant hours of model calls:
it now runs four at a time, and one owner's new numbers are enriched up to 200
a day — every number is still saved and scored.

